# Accepted findings, each with the reason. Review this file when the platform
# stops being a local lab.

# AVD-AWS-0088 / AVD-AWS-0132: S3 bucket encrypted with SSE-S3 rather than KMS.
# LocalStack Community does not implement KMS, so there is no key to point at.
AVD-AWS-0132

# AVD-AWS-0089: S3 access logging not enabled. Logging the audit bucket into
# another bucket in a mock has no value and doubles the storage.
AVD-AWS-0089

# AVD-AWS-0086..0087: public access block is configured; Trivy flags the
# account-level setting, which does not exist in LocalStack.
AVD-AWS-0094

# AVD-DS-0002: the CUDA k3s image runs as root. k3s needs it - it manages
# containerd, CNI and kubelet inside the node container.
AVD-DS-0002

# --- rendered manifests (scanned from the repo root, same ignore file) --------

# AVD-KSV-0014: readOnlyRootFilesystem is deliberately not enforced - the model
# runtime and the gateway touch more of the filesystem than is worth auditing
# in a local lab. Mirrors the no-read-only-root-fs exclusion in .kube-linter.yaml.
AVD-KSV-0014

# AVD-KSV-0109: false positive. The LiteLLM ConfigMap keys named "password" hold
# os.environ/... references read at runtime from a Secret-backed env var, not
# secret values.
AVD-KSV-0109
